---
name: playwright-smart-run
description: Run Playwright E2E tests against the dev/staging/production server without overloading. Handles cold-start retries, concurrency tuning, scoped test selection, k3s-vs-cloud config, and result triage. Avoids the "158 failed → dev server OOM" cascade.
triggers: when the user says "run e2e tests", "run playwright", "test the dev server", "test the live site", "k3s e2e", "test k3s standby", "run smoke tests", "test homepage"
---

# Playwright Smart Run

## Configs

| Target | Config | Base URL | When to use |
|---|---|---|---|
| Local dev | `playwright.config.mts` (default) | `http://localhost:4000` | Iterating on a feature |
| Pi k3s standby | `playwright.k3s.config.mts` | live cloudless.gr behind Pi path | Post-Pi-deploy validation |
| Production | `playwright.production.config.mts` | live cloudless.gr | Smoke after Lambda deploy |

## Concurrency rules of thumb

| Target | Workers | Why |
|---|---|---|
| Dev (Turbopack) | **2** | Turbopack compilation is single-threaded per route; more workers = thrashing |
| k3s live | 4 | Pi serving has fixed capacity |
| Production live | 6 (default) | Lambda scales horizontally |

## Smoke set (always run first)

```bash
cd /home/tbaltzakis/code/cloudless.gr
pnpm exec playwright test \
  e2e/api-routes.spec.ts \
  e2e/api-auth.spec.ts \
  e2e/homepage.spec.ts \
  e2e/security-headers.spec.ts \
  --project=chromium \
  --workers=2 \
  --reporter=line
```

Takes ~30s. If smoke fails, don't bother running the full suite — fix smoke first.

## Full local suite (after smoke passes)

```bash
# Warm up the server first (cold compile)
curl -s http://localhost:4000/en > /dev/null
curl -s http://localhost:4000/api/health > /dev/null

# Then run
pnpm exec playwright test \
  --project=chromium \
  --workers=2 \
  --reporter=line 2>&1 | tail -20
```

The `--workers=2` is critical for dev mode — running with default 6 workers overwhelms Turbopack and causes cascading 500s (the famous "158 failed" pattern). Workers=2 → ~5 minutes total. Workers=6 → server OOM, half the tests fail.

## k3s live tests

```bash
# These hit https://cloudless.gr via Pi path — no local server needed
pnpm test:k3s:smoke               # 10 tests, ~20s — sanity check
pnpm test:k3s                     # full 136-test suite, ~2 min
```

Common k3s failures:
- **React #418 hydration error** on `/en`: Lambda is serving but a route has a Date-in-render or similar SSR mismatch. Check `Footer.tsx` for `new Date()` without `suppressHydrationWarning`.
- **/api/auth/session 500**: missing `AUTH_TRUST_HOST` — see `lambda-env-check` skill.
- **logs.cloudless.gr ENOTFOUND from GH runner**: tunnel subdomain not resolvable from runner IP — test should skip, not fail. Already patched in `dns-resolution.spec.ts`.

## Triage failures fast

```bash
# Show only failing test names from a run
pnpm exec playwright test --project=chromium --reporter=line 2>&1 | grep -E "✗|failed"

# Trace a specific failure
pnpm exec playwright show-trace test-results/.../trace.zip

# Just rerun the failed ones
pnpm exec playwright test --last-failed --project=chromium
```

## What NOT to do

- Don't run full suite at `--workers=6` against the dev server — 158-failure cascade
- Don't run k3s tests in parallel with a deploy in progress
- Don't include `e2e/customer-behavior.spec.ts` `@mutating` tests against production — they actually subscribe emails / send messages
- Don't trust a single retry — if a test is flaky 2/3 runs, it's a real bug

## When dev server returns 500 mid-test

The dev server is dead. Restart per `dev-server-doctor` skill, then warm:

```bash
pkill -f "next dev"; sleep 2
cd /home/tbaltzakis/code/cloudless.gr && pnpm dev &
sleep 5
for r in /en /en/services /en/contact /api/health; do
  curl -s -o /dev/null "http://localhost:4000${r}"
done
# Now safe to re-run tests
```
